      <activity id="1967342a-7899-503a-a6c7-542053992121" activityNameId="a3848678-b01a-599c-ab23-30ef86b08e81" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Door frame, inner, steel, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Door frame, inner, steel, at plant
Data are based on a door leaf of 0.9m x 2m and scaled to 1m2 door. 1m2 of steel door frame weighs 12kg. The bill of materials is based on data from door manufactures and Werner et al. 1997.;
UUID: abe7515a-1847-3bfa-8070-9ff014dae409
Included are the materials used in an inner steel door frame (without surface treatment). Production losses and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: Data apply to the supply in Switzerland.
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 2 door producers in Switzerland. In addition the data from Werner et al. 1997 were used. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_abe7515a-1847-3bfa-8070-9ff014dae409.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
